title: get-refs reports success for a ref that does not exist, emitting an empty file
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`Cmd/GetRefs.pm:55-60` never checks whether `read_ref` returned anything:

    karr get-refs does/not/exist.md
    # stderr: Fetched refs/does/not/exist.md
    # stdout: one empty line
    # rc=0

So `karr get-refs spec.md > spec.md` silently produces an empty file and reports
success — a data-destroying shape for the documented "helper refs outside the
board" workflow.

Expected per ADR 0002: exit 1 with "ref not found" (runtime failure).
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
